why Every Horde quest of Krol'dok Stronghold in one run, with the Riverglades chain that opens them.

# Krol'dok Stronghold's Horde quests in one guide: Rog'mar's chain through
# Riverglades that opens them, one run through the dungeon, then the
# hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up wherever
# the chain stands.
#
# The chain, every quest a lead-in of the dungeon's three in the data:
# Krom'rosh's 93786 A Message in Blood and 93787 Food for the Taking -> 94483
# Show Them How It's Done; Tran'gul's 94680 Twilight Missives and 94672
# Encroaching Twilight -> 94727 Digging for Answers (to Clubtoe) -> 95417 The
# Purple Ones (to the Twilight Brute) -> 95601 The Purple Ones, and Clubtoe's
# 95602 Sickening Lights -> 95427 Twilight No More! -> 95418 Spread the Word
# (to Tran'gul) -> 95420 Land of Giants (to Clugfist) -> 95424 Might Makes
# Right and 95425 Unworthy Champion -> 95428 Clugfist's Decree (to Krom'rosh)
# -> 94744 The Wayward Warrior (to Da'grosh) -> 94745 Carving a Path and 94748
# Break Their Chains -> 94768 Bring Me His Head. Then Da'grosh's 94975 A Token
# of Vengeance (15 Cultist Ears) and 95278 It Is Time, Brother... (to
# Krom'rosh), Krom'rosh's 94968 Eye of Mugg and Tran'gul's 94972 Tome of
# Twilight. Inside, Tunk's Krol'dok Moulding (item 267137) starts 94973
# Krol'dok Moulding, for Kreza Darkthorn, who gives 94974 Key Ingredients.
#
# Left out: nothing of the Horde's. QuestieDB 1.1.4 also lists 95056 Krol'dok
# No More!, with no giver, ender or objective: nothing to write it from.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses or Tunk inside, so their goals
# stand at the door (@36.9,44.1) with `group 5`. The bosses come in the order
# of the client's dungeon journal (Slavecrusher Grox, Twilight Commander
# Zarmok, Handler Ashka, Nar'gurk, Overseer Mugg), not of a recorded run.
# Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group that takes them in
# another order still gets each step ticked. Riverglades has only Forever's
# map frame, so typed coordinates are `coords live`.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The scouts' and the ritual circles' spots are
#   the data's for those objectives.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - What drops where: the reference data: the Cultist Ears from the Twilight
#   Grunts and Warlocks and Zarmok, the tome from Nar'gurk, the eye from Mugg,
#   the moulding from Tunk (an elite inside).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   40 to 47).
# - Mob levels from data/forever set the waits: the ritualists 39 to 41, the
#   maulers 41 to 42, the Twilight on the western front 42 to 44, Overlord
#   Kilgar 46 (an elite).
# INGAME: where inside does Tunk stand?

